(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #155: a variable's type is fixed at its declaration,
 so a file opened or declared under a buffer's or a value's name is refused,
 in a branch and at the top level alike.)

a buffer called cupboard is "ab".
a buffer called pantry is "cd".
a value called larder is "ef".
a buffer called cellar is "gh".
a number called gate is 1.
If gate is 1 then,
    open a file called cupboard for writing at "cupboard.txt",
    Close cupboard.
open a file called pantry for writing at "pantry.txt".
open a file called larder for writing at "larder.txt".
a file called cellar is "cellar.txt".
Print "size {cupboard's size}".
